// Polities: chiefdoms and states (milestone 4). Runs once a year, after seafaring.
// Polities are organizations (the "organizations" table): each has a capital, a level (chiefdom
// or state), a temperament, and a set of positions left empty until named people come in
// milestone 6. Each land cell is ruled by at most one polity.
{
  // Temperament, drawn when a polity is founded: aggression (how readily it goes to war), greed
  // (how much tribute it takes) and expansion (how readily it draws in its neighbours). Each is
  // exp(temperamentSpread * a standard normal draw), kept between minTemperament and
  // maxTemperament, so most lie between about 0.7 and 1.4 and the typical one is 1.
  "temperamentSpread": 0.35,
  "minTemperament": 0.4,
  "maxTemperament": 2.5,

  // Positions every polity has, in order. They hold nobody until named people come (milestone 6).
  "positions": [ "Ruler", "Heir", "General" ],

  // Founding (milestone 4, step 2). Each year a settlement no polity rules may found a chiefdom
  // when it holds at least foundPeople people (settlements.json: a share of its cell's people),
  // farming has stood in its cell at least foundSettledYears, and its store holds grain for at
  // least foundSurplusYears of its cell's people. The yearly chance is foundChance times the
  // people in its cell and the neighbouring ones over crowdPeople (at most 1).
  "foundPeople": 900,
  "foundSettledYears": 3000,
  "foundSurplusYears": 0.5,
  "foundChance": 0.001,
  "crowdPeople": 50000,

  // Reach: the most a polity's cells may cost to reach from its capital, as trade carries goods
  // over land (trade.json: 1 a cell of lowland, more on hills and mountains, half along rivers;
  // less where the capital uses the wheel or riding). Cells beyond it are let go.
  "chiefdomReach": 4,
  "stateReach": 7,

  // Growing, every month: a polity draws in each unruled settlement within its reach with a
  // yearly chance (spread over the twelve months) of joinChance times its expansion
  // (temperament) times (1 - cost / reach), times unlinkedJoinFactor unless one of its
  // settlements trades with it; it then also rules the
  // unruled land on the way to it and next to it. Reach here runs only over the polity's own and
  // unruled land, never across another polity's. An unruled cell within reach with at least
  // claimNeighbours of its six neighbours ruled by the polity is claimed. A polity's land always
  // joins its capital: land cut off (by war or a split) breaks away, its large settlements
  // becoming successors (see below).
  "joinChance": 0.02,
  "unlinkedJoinFactor": 0.5,
  "claimNeighbours": 4,

  // A chiefdom that rules at least statePeople people and stateSettlements settlements is a
  // state; a state that falls below stateKeepShare of either is a chiefdom again.
  "statePeople": 300000,
  "stateSettlements": 15,
  "stateKeepShare": 0.5,

  // Tribute (step 3). Each year every ruled settlement but the capital gives the capital this share
  // of each good people use in its store (food, everyday goods and luxuries; raw materials such as
  // tin and copper stay to be traded and worked), times the polity's greed, times (1 - cost /
  // reach) so far ones give less, times (1 - its people's unrest), at most maxTributeShare.
  "tributeShare": 0.15,
  "maxTributeShare": 0.5,

  // The elite and soldiers live in the capital, drawn from its farmers (and sent back) staffChangeRate
  // of the way each year: elite eliteShare of the people the polity rules; soldiers
  // peaceSoldierShare of them, or borderSoldierShare where it borders another polity, times its
  // aggression; both together no more than last year's grain tribute feeds (a load of grain feeds
  // a person a year), and no more than maxStaffShare of the capital's people.
  "eliteShare": 0.01,
  "peaceSoldierShare": 0.005,
  "borderSoldierShare": 0.02,
  "staffChangeRate": 0.2,
  "maxStaffShare": 0.3,

  // Unrest, a condition of every group (0 to 1), moves unrestRate of the way each year toward
  // hungerUnrest x (1 - food met) + needsUnrest x (1 - everyday needs met) + tributeUnrest x the
  // share its settlement gave in tribute, at most 1.
  "unrestRate": 0.1,
  "hungerUnrest": 1.0,
  "needsUnrest": 0.2,
  "tributeUnrest": 1.5,

  // War (step 4). A polity at war raises soldiers toward warSoldierShare of its people (times its
  // aggression) instead of the shares above.
  "warSoldierShare": 0.04,

  // Strength: the soldiers in the capital times 1 + weaponStrength x the weapons in the capital's
  // store per soldier (bronze weapons count twice; at most maxWeaponsPerSoldier), so a fully armed
  // army with copper counts 1.5 and with bronze 2, plus a levy of militiaShare of the capital's people.
  // At a contested cell, each side's strength is
  // scaled by max(minDistanceFactor, 1 - cost from its capital / its reach); chariots (attack)
  // multiply an attacker's strength on open lowland, fortifications (defence) a defended
  // settlement's and its neighbouring cells' (a walled town shelters the country around it),
  // and the defender adds militiaShare of the cell's people.
  "weaponStrength": 0.5,
  "maxWeaponsPerSoldier": 2,
  "minDistanceFactor": 0.25,
  "militiaShare": 0.01,

  // Declaring war: once a year each polity at peace weighs each neighbour at peace that it has not
  // fought for peaceYears: aggression x (its strength over the neighbour's - 1, the ratio at most
  // maxStrengthRatio) + hungerWar x its capital farmers' unmet food + covetWar x (the neighbour's
  // share of the grain in the two capitals - 1/2). The strongest case above warThreshold leads to
  // war with chance warChance a year.
  "warThreshold": 0.6,
  "warChance": 0.2,
  "maxStrengthRatio": 4,
  "hungerWar": 1.0,
  "covetWar": 0.5,
  "peaceYears": 20,

  // Each year of war every cell along the border is contested: the side across takes it with
  // chance takeRate x its local strength / both, if the cell is within its reach. Each side loses
  // soldierLoss of its soldiers times the other's share of the strength (the attacker's counting
  // its chariots, the defender's the walls of its capital), and every contested cell civilianLoss
  // of its people. A taken
  // settlement loses burnShare of its store and plunderShare goes to the taker's capital; with
  // chance razeChance it is razed: razeDeaths of its people die and its store is lost. Taking the
  // enemy's capital conquers it: it ends, and the conqueror rules its cells within reach.
  "takeRate": 0.3,
  "soldierLoss": 0.2,
  "civilianLoss": 0.02,
  "burnShare": 0.5,
  "plunderShare": 0.25,
  "razeChance": 0.03,
  "razeDeaths": 0.6,

  // Peace: when either side's exhaustion (deaths over its people when the war began, plus the
  // share of its cells it has lost) reaches exhaustionLimit, or after maxWarYears. The less
  // exhausted side wins.
  "exhaustionLimit": 0.3,
  "maxWarYears": 15,

  // Collapse (step 5). Each year a polity's cohesion is 1 - cohesionUnrest x its people's unrest -
  // cohesionFamine x their unmet food - cohesionStretch x how far they live from the capital (cost
  // over reach, averaged over its people) - cohesionWar x its exhaustion in a war under way -
  // cohesionDefeat if it lost a war in the last defeatYears.
  "cohesionUnrest": 1.5,
  "cohesionFamine": 1.0,
  "cohesionStretch": 0.65,
  "cohesionWar": 1.0,
  "cohesionDefeat": 0.2,
  "defeatYears": 20,

  // Below splitThreshold a polity splits with chance splitChance x (splitThreshold - cohesion) /
  // splitThreshold a year: the land at least splitDistance of its reach from the capital, and each
  // settlement whose unrest is at least revoltUnrest with the land next to it, breaks away. In turn
  // the largest settlement breaking away with at least successorPeople people living in it (as
  // foundPeople counts them) founds a successor
  // chiefdom, which takes the breaking land within its reach, up to maxSuccessors of them; the rest
  // falls back to no rule. A polity that loses its capital (abandoned or conquered) breaks up the
  // same way, all of it.
  "splitThreshold": 0.42,
  "splitChance": 0.05,
  "splitDistance": 0.5,
  "revoltUnrest": 0.4,
  "successorPeople": 1500,
  "maxSuccessors": 2
}
